{#
  The success page after converting — v6's own port of v4's
  upload-converted.html. Reached from the check page via the POST-then-GET
  redirect in controller.js, so refreshing doesn't resubmit.

  "View the guidance" goes to /v6/editor-2-3-view (no ?id=) — the v6
  editor entry point (every such link across v6 now points here rather
  than at /v6/editor-experiment — see the audit this was built from) —
  rather than v4's own read-only guide-view.html — a deliberate
  difference, confirmed directly rather than assumed: the task this flow
  was built from wants the converted guidance genuinely viewable/editable,
  not read-only, and this is the same fallback (fixed sample content)
  "Review and fix the issues" already used on the retired v2-based version
  of this flow. It does not create a real tracked Draft document — this
  page's own guideName is session-only, and the converted guidance does
  not appear on the unified hub's Editing tab (an explicitly confirmed
  scope choice, not an oversight). "Convert another document" restarts the
  upload step.
#}
{% extends "common/layouts/content.njk" %}

{% from "govuk/components/panel/macro.njk" import govukPanel %}
{% from "govuk/components/button/macro.njk" import govukButton %}

{% set pageName = "Guidance converted" %}

{% block columns %}

  {{ govukPanel({
    titleText: "Guidance converted",
    text: guideName
  }) }}

  <h2 class="govuk-heading-m">What happens next</h2>

  <p class="govuk-body">
    Your document is now markdown in the hub, saved as a draft. Only you can
    see it until it is reviewed and published.
  </p>

  <p class="govuk-body">
    Have a look at how it converted before you take it any further.
  </p>

  {{ govukButton({
    text: "View the guidance",
    href: "/v6/editor-2-3-view"
  }) }}

  <p class="govuk-body">
    <a class="govuk-link" href="/v6/create-guidance/upload">Convert another document</a>
  </p>

{% endblock %}
